        <briefdescription>
<para>The epsilon value used for floating-point comparisons. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This instance member defines the precision for comparisons. It is set via the constructor, either explicitly or computed as a default based on the number of decimal digits in the value. Each instance carries its own epsilon, so two <computeroutput>value&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput> objects with different precisions do not interfere with each other. </para>
